        "message": {
          "role": "assistant",
          "content": "{\n  \"cvss_vector\": \"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:H/SA:N\",\n  \"aivss\": {\n    \"LC\": \"D\",\n    \"CP\": \"C\",\n    \"AP\": \"C\",\n    \"RH\": \"P\",\n    \"ES\": \"W\"\n  },\n  \"rationales\": {\n    \"LC\": \"The unauthenticated endpoint accepts goals without content validation, and the text enters the privileged system prompt as an explicit override (finbot-ctf-demo/src/routes/admin.py:90-109; finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:69-71). This is direct language control rather than ingestion through retrieved content.\",\n    \"CP\": \"The goals are committed to a durable configuration row and subsequently change standing system-prompt behavior (finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:735-748; finbot-ctf-demo/src/models/vendor.py:105). This is cross-session objective persistence, not merely re-retrieval of unchanged source material.\",\n    \"AP\": \"Influence passes from the model into the fixed, in-process tool dispatcher under FinBot's existing authority (finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:347-361). The briefing establishes no separate agent or tenant execution domain; effects on other vendors' database records are subsequent-system impacts, not by themselves lateral agent propagation.\",\n    \"RH\": \"The agent can write the environment's processing-success proxy by marking an invoice approved and payment_processed true, then terminating processing through approve_invoice (finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:409-458; finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:150-226). The walkthrough proposes testing but supplies no human-verified production-equivalent episode, supporting Possible rather than Demonstrated (finbot-ctf-demo/docs/FinBot-CTF-walkthrough-goal-manipulation.md:152-170).\",\n    \"ES\": \"Although tool identities are fixed, arguments receive no independent validation beyond JSON parsing, and approval lacks an independently enforced amount or review constraint (finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:347-361; finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:409-458). Consequently, reachable security-relevant tool arguments remain unconstrained on this path, satisfying Wide.\",\n    \"CVSS\": \"For the documented model-driven path, public network binding and the unauthenticated goals endpoint support AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N: the attacker can perform both requests without another person's participation (finbot-ctf-demo/gunicorn.conf.py:4; finbot-ctf-demo/src/routes/admin.py:90-109; finbot-ctf-demo/src/routes/vendor.py:69-110). Persistent replacement of privileged objectives gives VI:H, while unauthorized high-value approval and payment-state changes in the subsequent database give SI:H; the attacker does not already own the business-wide configuration or its approval authority (finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:735-748; finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:409-458; finbot-ctf-demo/src/main.py:35-65). This path establishes neither disclosure nor availability loss, so VC/VA/SC/SA are N.\"\n  },\n  \"evidence\": {\n    \"LC\": [\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/routes/admin.py:90-109\",\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:69-71\"\n    ],\n    \"CP\": [\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:735-748\",\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/models/vendor.py:105\",\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:69-71\"\n    ],\n    \"AP\": [\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:347-361\",\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:228-345\"\n    ],\n    \"RH\": [\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:409-458\",\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:150-226\",\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/docs/FinBot-CTF-walkthrough-goal-manipulation.md:152-170\"\n    ],\n    \"ES\": [\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:228-345\",\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:347-361\",\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:409-458\"\n    ],\n    \"CVSS\": [\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/gunicorn.conf.py:4\",\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/routes/admin.py:90-109\",\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/routes/vendor.py:69-110\",\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:735-748\",\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:409-458\",\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/main.py:35-65\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"confidence\": {\n    \"LC\": \"high\",\n    \"CP\": \"high\",\n    \"AP\": \"medium\",\n    \"RH\": \"medium\",\n    \"ES\": \"medium\",\n    \"CVSS\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  \"rh_facts\": {\n    \"reachable_proxy\": true,\n    \"isolation_verified\": null,\n    \"verified_episodes\": 0,\n    \"episodes_reviewed\": 0,\n    \"locus\": \"environment\"\n  },\n  \"automatable\": \"Yes\",\n  \"automatable_rationale\": \"For the documented path, goals updates and invoice submissions are ordinary unauthenticated HTTP requests, and approval requires no human confirmation (finbot-ctf-demo/src/routes/admin.py:90-109; finbot-ctf-demo/src/routes/vendor.py:69-110; finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:409-458). Model variability can affect reliability but does not prevent automated execution.\",\n  \"technical_impact\": \"Total\",\n  \"technical_impact_rationale\": \"The documented attack replaces FinBot's standing objectives for every later invoice and defeats the core approval-policy protection until the configuration is reset (finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:735-748; finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:69-71). Total refers to control of the assessed decision-making function, not proven host takeover or actual bank transfers.\",\n  \"applicability_as_implemented\": {\n    \"model_directed_goal_pursuit\": false,\n    \"selects_or_sequences_actions\": false,\n    \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n    \"rationale\": \"The supplied default deployment does not provision an OpenAI API key; client initialization failure selects rule-based fallback processing rather than model-directed tool selection (finbot-ctf-demo/render.yaml:1-17; finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:14-21; finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:772-877). These answers describe that supplied default; externally provisioning credentials would enable the model-driven branch.\"\n  },\n  \"applicability_as_modeled\": {\n    \"model_directed_goal_pursuit\": true,\n    \"selects_or_sequences_actions\": true,\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"rationale\": \"The documented agent pursues natural-language invoice-processing goals using gpt-4.1-mini and chooses tools automatically across an execution loop of up to five iterations (finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:14-21; finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:150-226). The walkthrough specifically models changed objectives causing subsequent invoice-approval decisions (finbot-ctf-demo/docs/FinBot-CTF-walkthrough-goal-manipulation.md:152-170).\"\n  },\n  \"refusal\": null\n}",
